 "voiceover": "[excited, conversational] Wait — an AI may have just made decades of computer science research irrelevant. [curious] OpenAI and Anthropic both say their AI disproved the exponential time hypothesis, an idea hundreds of studies rely on. It isn't independently verified yet. But one professor told WIRED it could make around 50 of his papers pointless or in need of a revisit.\n\n[amused] Meanwhile, Google's AI Mode won't say who won the 2020 US election. Fast Company reports that in other countries, it does.\n\n[serious] And US senators Wyden and Markey wrote to Mark Zuckerberg about \"serious privacy and safety risks\" in Meta's AI glasses. They want answers by November 26.\n\n[playful] Over at Wikipedia's nonprofit, Wikimedia says training AI on copyrighted work should be fair use, but chatbots copying it back to users shouldn't.\n\n[confident] So AI is shaking up science, politics, privacy and copyright, all at once.\n\n[playful, warm] Send this to the friend who thinks AI is just a chatbot.",
